 ## Overview
-A Conditional Radiance Field extends the standard NeRF representation to model an entire object class (e.g., chairs) rather than a single static scene, using instance-specific latent vectors for shape and appearance to enable editing and interpolation [S1, S2]. It differs from standard NeRF by decoupling instance-specific details into latent codes $\mathbf{z}$ while storing shared class information in the network parameters, allowing the radiance field characteristics to be altered via latent variable manipulation [S2].
+A Conditional Radiance Field extends the standard NeRF representation to model an entire object class (e.g., chairs) rather than a single static scene, using instance-specific latent vectors for shape and appearance to enable editing and interpolation [S1, S2]. It builds on [Latent Code Conditioning](16345-latent-code-conditioning.md) by decoupling instance-specific details into latent codes $\mathbf{z}$ while storing shared class information in the network parameters, allowing the radiance field characteristics to be altered via latent variable manipulation [S2].
 
